data.content:
This is caused by **Microsoft.OpenApi upgrading from v1 to v2** in .NET 10. Here are the breaking changes and fixes:

## 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` types removed
The entire `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace is gone. Use `System.Text.Json.Nodes` instead:

```csharp
// OLD
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// NEW
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

## 2. `Schema.Nullable` removed
Nullability is now a flag on `Schema.Type` (which is a `[Flags]` enum `JsonSchemaType`):

```csharp
// OLD
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// NEW — remove the Null flag from Type
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

You'll need `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;` (which you already have).

## 3. `OpenApiReference.Type` → `OpenApiReference.Type` uses new enum
`ReferenceType` was renamed/consolidated:

```csharp
// OLD
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }

// NEW
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
```

This one **still compiles** — the enum value name is preserved, but verify the import is `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models`.

## 4. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a `Dictionary`
You can no longer use collection-initializer syntax with `[scheme] = scopes`:

```csharp
// OLD
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// NEW
var requirement = new OpenApiSecurityRequirement();
requirement.Schemes.Add(oAuthScheme, scopes);
operation.Security = [requirement];
```

## Fixed code (complete)

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    var requirement = new OpenApiSecurityRequirement();
    requirement.Schemes.Add(oAuthScheme, scopes);
    operation.Security = [requirement];

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of namespace changes:**
| v1 (OpenApi 1.x) | v2 (OpenApi 2.x) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` + `OpenApiString` | `System.Text.Json.Nodes` + `JsonValue.Create()` |
| `Schema.Nullable = bool` | `Schema.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `new OpenApiSecurityRequirement { [scheme] = list }` | `requirement.Schemes.Add(scheme, list)` |
